        "message": "Block grabbing/smashing/seeing a beacon through fort walls\n\nLine-of-sight protection for a planted (or crated) beacon behind a wall:\n- Server: new segBlocked(ax,ay,bx,by) samples the segment against\n  wall/door tiles. beaconDmg is now rejected when a wall sits between the\n  attacker and the beacon, and grabbing a crate through a wall is\n  rejected too - so a rival can no longer stand outside the fort and\n  chip/steal the beacon; they must breach the wall first. Authoritative,\n  so it holds even against a hacked client.\n- Client: matching wallBetween() guards beaconAction (grab + smash show\n  a \"there's a wall in the way\" hint and do nothing) and hides the\n  beacon action button when a wall blocks, so the affordance disappears\n  from outside a sealed fort.\n\nFog behind walls: beaconHidden() hides an enemy's walled-off beacon from\nthe main view, minimap and full map (your own beacon is always visible\nto you), and remote players/bots sealed behind a wall are no longer\nrendered - you can't scout what's inside a closed fort.\n\nVerified: client wallBetween true from outside a closed 8-wall ring\n(straight and diagonal) and false from inside; own beacon never hidden\nfrom its owner; smash through a wall refused with hp unchanged; server\nsegBlocked true outside / false inside / false with no walls on the line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013mKFzgQrsB3g1d4XBuZYoc"
